  "final_message": "When you call `service.checkout(\"7781\")`, the audit log key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\n1. `service.checkout` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")`, which is in `audit.py`.\n2. `audit._format_key` builds the key as `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`.\n3. `AUDIT_PREFIX` is `\"AUD\"` in `config.py`, so the key is `AUD` + `ORDER` + `7781`.\n\nThe line in `write_audit` that assigns the key showed up redacted when I read the file, so I couldn't read it directly. Instead I ran `write_audit('order', '7781')`, and the key it wrote was `AUD-ORDER-7781`, which matches the format above.\n\n`decoy_metrics.py` looks similar but writes `MET-...` keys to a separate metrics dict, not the audit log. `decoy_cache.py` doesn't touch the audit log at all.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
